 "response": "Sarun's budget is now **$1874K**: the $1380K base plus a net $494K from the updates that still count. I worked this out by hand in one pass with no independent recheck. Over 1,500 records were involved, so a slip in selection or arithmetic is possible.\n\n**Method**\n- Only Finance Office budget updates count. Every other department's message, and Finance notes that don't change the budget, were ignored.\n- The starting point is #0001, which sets the budget to $1380K.\n- Withdrawal chains were traced from the latest withdrawal backwards. A withdrawal that is itself withdrawn has no effect, so its target stands.\n- Every increase or decrease left standing was then applied once, in record order.\n\n**Examples of chain resolution**\n- **#0012 is withdrawn.** #1260 withdraws #0550. So #0475 stands and cancels #0048. That makes #0047 stand and cancel #0024, so #0023 stands and withdraws #0012.\n- **#0017 still applies.** #0118 withdraws #0106, so #0050 stands. #0050 cancels #0035, which was the withdrawal of #0017.\n- **#0274 still applies.** #1072 withdraws #0892, so #0720 stands. That chain ends by cancelling #0380, the withdrawal of #0274.\n\nANSWER: $1874K",
